# Auto-tune: uniform behaviour for all algorithms and formats

When editing **auto-tune** (hyperparameter tuning, MLQA, stability, search space, Phase 1/2 in `ml.tuning` or `ml.auto_tune`):

1. **No algorithm-only changes**  
   Do not add or change behaviour for a single ML algorithm (e.g. only `quantile` or only `mlp`) unless the **same** logic is applied to every other algorithm used in auto-tune. Prefer one data- or config-driven path for all algorithms.

2. **No format-only changes**  
   Do not add or change behaviour for a single match format (e.g. only `T20` or only `T20I`) unless the **same** logic is applied to every format. Prefer logic driven by dataset/training parameters (e.g. `n_samples`, config) so all formats are handled uniformly.

3. **Before finishing**  
   Check: “Does this treat any algorithm or format specially?” If yes, either generalize so it applies to all, or document a minimal, justified exception.

Full note: **ml-service/ml/tuning/AGENTS_AUTO_TUNE.md**.
